Additional Comments on the placement of the morse elements . . . 

The location of the morse required some assumptions.  Here's my line of 
thinking. . . 

Assumption One:  The width of the copper elements appears to be uniform 
throughout and the seams are parallel.  I used the seams as a coordinate
system.   

Assumption Two:  Jim Gillogy's pictures were taken within an hour or so of each
other.  (This let me use shadow patterns for reference).

With those assumptions . . . let's take each morse element . . .

VIRTUALLY INVISIBLE: This is a gimme . . . given it's location right next to
the walkway it was easily to place.  It also allowed me to establish the offset
of the morse from the axis of the walkway, which coincidentally is an east west
axis.  

SHADOW FORCES: Ditto of above.  

T IS YOUR POSITON: Clearly located at the lodestone on the south outcropping
(compass rose). Another gimme. 

Only four left to place: SOS, RQ, LUCID MEMORY and DIGETAL INTERPRETATU

LUCID MEMORY:  The third element of the north outcropping has too many 
letters for SOS and RQ, so I had to decide whether this was LUCID MEMORY or
DIGETAL INTERPRETATU.  This was a little more difficult to place until I 
realized that the shadows (subtle shadings and absense there of) could help me
position these two.  The north end of the north outcropping is shaded by trees
in Jim G's pix. the pic of LUCID MEMORY includes shadows in a similar location.
Applying assumption 2, I placed LUCID MEMORY as the next element on the north
outcropping.   I am hoping that Jim or Elonka or someone who has been on site
can verify this placement.  I am about 90% confident this is correct. 

DIGETAL INTERPRETATU: Jim G's picture of this is in direct sulight with no 
shadows all.  The only place left in direct sun was on the south outcropping
above the compass rose.  I'd place this at an 80% confidence level.  Again, I'm
hoping that some one who has been there can say, "Yes . . that's it!"

RQ and SOS:  Both of Jim G's photos show shadows from trees like the north end
of the north outcropping, so I placed them there, using the relationship to
the seams (assumption 1) to establish their locations.  SOS is clearly closer
to the ground than RQ, so I placed RQ higher on the outcropping.   There is 
another seam available to place these elements, so I could be off on these
two,  but I think the general location (the north edge) and the relation of the
two (RQ elevated higher than SOS) is correct.  




